# No Invented Business Data

## Rule

Do not invent Nelna operational values, including but not limited to:

- Temperature limits or product temperature classes
- CCP / OPRP classifications
- Sites, departments, lines, rooms, or warehouses
- Shifts, night-shift operational-day definitions
- Products, SKUs, or packaging configurations
- Checklist items, frequencies, or pass/fail criteria
- Approval rules, hold rules, or release rules
- User counts, device inventories, or retention periods presented as fact
- Certification scheme claims not evidenced by owners

## Required practice

- Mark unconfirmed items as ASSUMPTION, DECISION REQUIRED, OWNER REQUIRED, or EVIDENCE REQUIRED.
- Every implemented business rule must identify business owner and evidence source.
- Stakeholder questionnaires and assumption registers are the capture mechanism for real values.
- Proposed MVP scope and NFRs remain proposed until approved.

## Documentation language

- Prefer “proposed”, “to be confirmed”, “owner required”, and “evidence required”.
- Do not present placeholders as approved Nelna facts.
- Do not copy or reuse operational content from any previous repository.
